From: edde746 <86283021+edde746@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] screenshot: correctly detect hardware frame

Backport of upstream mpv b7b9ec2 (PR #17186, fixes #17185), which is not
in a release yet. Since mpv 9b1d47e an mp_image of a hardware format
describes its software subformat in image->fmt, so the software
screenshot's "is this a hardware frame" check (image->fmt.flags &
MP_IMGFLAG_HWACCEL) is false for one: the VA-API frame went to libswscale
undownloaded and every screenshot failed with "Input image format vaapi
not supported by libswscale". That is the path whenever the VO cannot take
the screenshot itself, as with the render API on GLES (no tex_download):
Plezy's Linux player on the Steam Deck. The check now asks the image's
format.
---
  player/screenshot.c | 2 +-
  1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/player/screenshot.c b/player/screenshot.c
index c733a2b..32d10a0 100644
--- a/player/screenshot.c
+++ b/player/screenshot.c
@@ -377,7 +377,7 @@ static struct mp_image *screenshot_get(struct MPContext *mpctx, int mode,
     }
 
     // vo_get_current_frame() can return a hardware frame, which we have to download first.
-    if (image && image->fmt.flags & MP_IMGFLAG_HWACCEL) {
+    if (image && IMGFMT_IS_HWACCEL(image->imgfmt)) {
         struct mp_image *nimage = mp_image_hw_download(image, NULL);
         talloc_free(image);
         if (!nimage)
